Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

DOS-PORT (patch 0108, Phase 10 W22-WB-E shutdown-hang triage). Adds
9 doskutsu_dbg_log bracket lines around each step of main.cpp's
shutdown sequence (lines ~702-713), so the operator's next iter's
PAUSESDL.LOG pinpoints exactly which step hangs by which numbered
line is LAST written.

Background -- sdl-engine STOP-and-ack'd what was originally going
to be SDL/0045 (dbg_log per-line fsync) because patches/SDL/0024
ALREADY adds per-line fsync (not per-flush). Their analysis: the
missing close-path lines in W22-WB-D PAUSESDL.LOG mean those
SDL-side lines NEVER FIRED -- so the hang is BEFORE the SDL
CloseDevice path, somewhere in the engine-side teardown chain.

Per team-lead 2026-05-07 dispatch this work shifts to the engine
side: drop bracket lines around each step in the engine's shutdown
sequence so we can see which step the engine reaches before the
hang (not the SDL CloseDevice that was originally suspected).

Cross-vendor decl pattern matches slot 0102 / 0103 / 0100:
  extern "C" void doskutsu_dbg_log(const char *fmt, ...);
declared at file scope (not function scope -- language-spec
restriction; first attempt placed it inside main() and gcc
rejected with "expected unqualified-id before string constant",
fixed to file scope which works cleanly).

doskutsu_dbg_log itself defined in vendor/SDL/src/video/dos/
SDL_dosdbg.c (SDL/0024-perf-wave-13-6-1-env-var-sdldbg-log-
filename); the per-line fsync there means each bracket call hits
disk before the next teardown step starts.

Bracket points (8 numbered + 1 final = 9 lines):
  [1/8] pre-game.tsc->Close
  [2/8] pre-game.close
  [3/8] pre-Carets::close
  [4/8] pre-input_close
  [5/8] pre-textbox.Deinit
  [6/8] pre-SoundManager::shutdown   <- slot 0106's new method
  [7/8] pre-Renderer::close
  [8/8] pre-SDL_Quit
  [final] post-SDL_Quit; engine teardown complete

If hang is in (e.g.) MidiScheduler::shutdown via SoundManager,
PAUSESDL.LOG should show "[5/8] pre-textbox.Deinit" and
"[6/8] pre-SoundManager::shutdown" present, no further bracket
lines. Operator can then narrow further within SoundManager::
shutdown if needed.

Smoke (DOSBox-X-fast):

  Per memory dosbox_not_behavioral_proxy_for_io.md: DOSBox-X
  cannot faithfully reproduce the shutdown hang (and pkill kills
  mid-run anyway, never triggering the in-game Quit path), so
  smoke validates only:
    (a) compile + link cleanly on top of slot 0107
    (b) all 9 bracket strings embedded in binary via strings-grep
    (c) engine launches normally (no init-time regression)

  Default smoke: 39 flips, no crashes. Engine starts cleanly with
  both slot 0107 (MIDI source dir env var) and slot 0108 (shutdown
  brackets) in tree. strings-grep confirms all 9 lines:
    "engine-shutdown[1/8]: pre-game.tsc->Close"
    "engine-shutdown[2/8]: pre-game.close"
    "engine-shutdown[3/8]: pre-Carets::close"
    "engine-shutdown[4/8]: pre-input_close"
    "engine-shutdown[5/8]: pre-textbox.Deinit"
    "engine-shutdown[6/8]: pre-SoundManager::shutdown"
    "engine-shutdown[7/8]: pre-Renderer::close"
    "engine-shutdown[8/8]: pre-SDL_Quit"
    "engine-shutdown[final]: post-SDL_Quit; engine teardown
     complete; control returning to main()"

  Real-HW iter is the essential validation gate. Operator's
  next iter (W22-WB-E) Quit path will produce numbered bracket
  lines in PAUSESDL.LOG up to the hang point. flush-instr can
  then identify the hanging step from the highest-numbered line
  written.

Out of scope (per team-lead "scope is exactly the path-switch
+ log line + docs entry" framing for 0107 + similar tightness
for 0108):
  - Bracket points within individual shutdown steps (e.g., 6.1
    pre-MidiScheduler::shutdown, 6.2 pre-Organya::shutdown) --
    only add if 0108's high-level brackets identify a
    specific step that needs further narrowing
  - SDL-side bracket logs (sdl-engine's lane; orthogonal)
---
 src/main.cpp | 31 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 31 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/main.cpp b/src/main.cpp
index e4392b0..502e943 100644
--- a/src/main.cpp
+++ b/src/main.cpp
@@ -31,6 +31,14 @@ using namespace NXE::Graphics;
 #include "screeneffect.h"
 #include "sound/SoundManager.h"
 #include "Utils/Logger.h"
+
+// patch 0108 (Phase 10 W22-WB-E shutdown-hang triage): cross-vendor
+// extern decl for doskutsu_dbg_log. Declared in vendor/SDL/src/video/
+// dos/SDL_dosdbg.h with printf-style varargs; internal SDL header not
+// on engine's public include path so we forward-declare at file scope
+// here. C linkage so the cross-vendor symbol resolution is mangling-
+// agnostic (matches slot 0100 / 0102 / 0103 cross-vendor extern pattern).
+extern "C" void doskutsu_dbg_log(const char *fmt, ...);
 using namespace NXE::Utils;
 
 #if defined(__SWITCH__)
@@ -699,18 +707,41 @@ int main(int argc, char *argv[])
   }
 
 shutdown:;
+  // patch 0108 (Phase 10 W22-WB-E shutdown-hang triage): bracket
+  // each teardown step with doskutsu_dbg_log so the operator's
+  // PAUSESDL.LOG pinpoints exactly which step hangs by which
+  // numbered line is LAST written. SDL/0024's per-line fsync
+  // means each call hits disk before the next step starts; if a
+  // step hangs (e.g., infinite spinwait in SDL_DOSMpu401Init's
+  // status-port poll on real DreamBlaster S2 hardware per
+  // W22-WB-D evidence), the highest-numbered "engine-shutdown[N/8]"
+  // line in the SDL log identifies the last successful step.
+  //
+  // Cross-vendor doskutsu_dbg_log declared at file scope above
+  // (per slot 0102/0103/0100 cross-vendor extern pattern).
+
+  doskutsu_dbg_log("engine-shutdown[1/8]: pre-game.tsc->Close");
   game.tsc->Close();
+  doskutsu_dbg_log("engine-shutdown[2/8]: pre-game.close");
   game.close();
+  doskutsu_dbg_log("engine-shutdown[3/8]: pre-Carets::close");
   Carets::close();
 
+  doskutsu_dbg_log("engine-shutdown[4/8]: pre-input_close");
   input_close();
+  doskutsu_dbg_log("engine-shutdown[5/8]: pre-textbox.Deinit");
   textbox.Deinit();
+  doskutsu_dbg_log("engine-shutdown[6/8]: pre-SoundManager::shutdown");
   NXE::Sound::SoundManager::getInstance()->shutdown();
+  doskutsu_dbg_log("engine-shutdown[7/8]: pre-Renderer::close");
   Renderer::getInstance()->close();
 #if defined(__SWITCH__)
   romfsExit();
 #endif
+  doskutsu_dbg_log("engine-shutdown[8/8]: pre-SDL_Quit");
   SDL_Quit();
+  doskutsu_dbg_log("engine-shutdown[final]: post-SDL_Quit; engine "
+                   "teardown complete; control returning to main()");
   return error;
 
 ingame_error:;
